{"name":"Washed Khaki","hex":"#cac2af","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"washed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of wash"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Ellipsis of washed up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/washed"},{"term":"khaki","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dull, yellowish-brown colour, the colour of dust.","Khaki green, a dull green colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dust-coloured; of the colour of dust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/khaki"}],"entries":[{"title":"Washed","blocks":[{"text":"\"Washed\" is a song recorded live by the American Christian music collective Elevation Rhythm. The song was released on September 19, 2025, through Elevation Worship Records, to digital download and streaming formats. It was written by Joe L. Barnes, Joshua Holiday, Mitch Wong, and Steven Furtick, while Holiday produced. \"Washed\" peaked at number 97 on the Billboard Hot 100 and number 1 on the Hot Christian Songs chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Elevation_Rhythm_Washed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washed"},{"title":"Khaki","blocks":[{"text":"The color khaki is a light shade of tan with a slight yellowish tinge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Marineoffiziere_in_Dakar_%281994%29.jpg/330px-Marineoffiziere_in_Dakar_%281994%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khaki"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/A_Tanaoli_of_the_Guides_%28Lumsden%27s%29_Infantry%2C_and_an_Afridi_Daffadar_of_the_Guides_Cavalry%2C_1908_%28c%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-A_Tanaoli_of_the_Guides_%28Lumsden%27s%29_Infantry%2C_and_an_Afridi_Daffadar_of_the_Guides_Cavalry%2C_1908_%28c%29_%28cro